This file used to sit at the bottom of LICENSE. It was moved out because
GitHub's license detection reads a file with anything appended to the MIT
text as "Other", and the licence here is plain MIT.

PractRand
    Chris Doty-Humphrey. The judge in every measurement in this
    repository, and NOT included here: it is downloaded and built from
    source, and it is subject to its own licence. Version 0.94, built
    with -std=gnu++14 and the return patch documented in
    rrc/PRACTRAND_FINDING.md.

The RRC test scheme
    Pelle Evensen. Rotate, reverse and complement disguises for counter
    streams. The scheme this entire rig is built on. Both external
    calibration weights are his published measurements: mix13's failure
    range and NASAM's pass at RRC-64-42.

Reference mixers and constants
    mix13 is Stafford's, fmix64 is Appleby's, moremur and NASAM are
    Evensen's, the wyhash pattern and the wyrand step are Wang Yi's.
    Where a constant comes from someone else's mixer, README.md says so
    at the place it is used.

The cost-axis comparison
    Martin Leitner-Ankerl's mixer benchmark
    (github.com/martinus/better-faster-stronger-mixer) is the prior art
    for measuring mixers against a cost axis. The figures attributed to
    him in costlimit/ were counted from his published tables and never
    re-measured here; literature/LITERATURE.md records that.
